From 46815dc5f364959b0485458e2578bb5875014b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sandbox: Allow rt_sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK) in all builds

pthread_create() in musl, and in glibc since 2.32, blocks signals with
rt_sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK) while it starts a thread, and then restores
the mask it saved with SIG_SETMASK. Neither checks whether the first
call worked. The sandbox allowed SIG_BLOCK only in fragile-hardening
and LTTng builds, so elsewhere the call failed with EPERM, and the
thread calling pthread_create() got whatever was on its stack as its
new signal mask.

Tor starts its cpuworker threads from the main thread after the sandbox
is installed, so the main thread could end up blocking SIGTERM, SIGINT
or SIGHUP, and Tor would ignore them.

This adds nothing to what the sandbox already permits: SIG_SETMASK is
already allowed, and it can install any mask.

Fixes bug 41060; bugfix on 0.2.5.1-alpha.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QfypjVN44TWb81ExDAokwk
---
 changes/bug41060          | 6 ++++++
 src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.c | 7 ++++---
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 changes/bug41060

diff --git a/changes/bug41060 b/changes/bug41060
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..56f3b43248
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/bug41060
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+  o Minor bugfixes (sandbox):
+    - With Sandbox enabled, stop Tor from sometimes ignoring SIGTERM,
+      SIGINT, and SIGHUP. The sandbox refused rt_sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK),
+      which pthread_create() uses in musl and in glibc 2.32 and later, so
+      starting a worker thread could leave the main thread with an
+      uninitialized signal mask. Fixes bug 41060; bugfix on 0.2.5.1-alpha.
diff --git a/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.c b/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.c
index b12df9f24c..04177c4944 100644
--- a/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.c
+++ b/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.c
@@ -1361,13 +1361,14 @@ sb_rt_sigprocmask(scmp_filter_ctx ctx, sandbox_cfg_t *filter)
   int rc = 0;
   (void) filter;
 
-#if defined(ENABLE_FRAGILE_HARDENING) || \
-    defined(USE_TRACING_INSTRUMENTATION_LTTNG)
+  /* pthread_create() in glibc (since 2.32) and musl blocks signals with
+   * SIG_BLOCK, and then restores the saved mask without checking whether
+   * that call worked. If we refuse SIG_BLOCK, the calling thread gets a
+   * garbage signal mask. */
   rc = seccomp_rule_add_1(ctx, SCMP_ACT_ALLOW, SCMP_SYS(rt_sigprocmask),
       SCMP_CMP(0, SCMP_CMP_EQ, SIG_BLOCK));
   if (rc)
     return rc;
-#endif
 
   rc = seccomp_rule_add_1(ctx, SCMP_ACT_ALLOW, SCMP_SYS(rt_sigprocmask),
       SCMP_CMP(0, SCMP_CMP_EQ, SIG_UNBLOCK));
-- 
2.43.0

